      "message": "Julio: The next test failure is caused by using `AOM_TUNE_IQ` in good-quality mode (see `kOnePassGood` at line 361):\n\n```\n20:32:28 [ RUN      ] AV1/ResizeCrashTest.TestRestorationFilterCrash/0\n20:32:28 /var/jenkins/workspace/libaom__per_commit-compile_sanitizers/sanitizer/address/aom/test/encode_test_driver.h:115: Failure\n20:32:28 Expected equality of these values:\n20:32:28   AOM_CODEC_OK\n20:32:28     Which is: 0\n20:32:28   res\n20:32:28     Which is: 4\n20:32:28 Codec does not implement requested capability\n20:32:29 /var/jenkins/workspace/libaom__per_commit-compile_sanitizers/sanitizer/address/aom/test/resize_test.cc:409: Failure\n20:32:29 Expected: RunLoop(\u0026video) doesn\u0027t generate new fatal failures in the current thread.\n20:32:29   Actual: it does.\n20:32:29 [  FAILED  ] AV1/ResizeCrashTest.TestRestorationFilterCrash/0, where GetParam() \u003d (0x55c1ff441040, 3) (1031 ms)\n```\n\nbecause of the following check in av1/av1_cx_iface.c:\n\n```\nstatic aom_codec_err_t handle_tuning(aom_codec_alg_priv_t *ctx,\n                                     struct av1_extracfg *extra_cfg) {\n  if (extra_cfg-\u003etuning \u003d\u003d AOM_TUNE_IQ ||\n      extra_cfg-\u003etuning \u003d\u003d AOM_TUNE_SSIMULACRA2) {\n    if (ctx-\u003ecfg.g_usage !\u003d AOM_USAGE_ALL_INTRA) return AOM_CODEC_INCAPABLE;\n```\n\nI can fix this by either\n- changing `kOnePassGood` to `kAllIntra` at line 361, or\n- changing `AOM_TUNE_IQ` to `AOM_TUNE_SSIM`.\n\nBoth changes can reproduce the heap-use-after-free error under AddressSanitizer. I think it is better to use `AOM_TUNE_SSIM` so that this test exercises inter-frame encoding. Do you agree?",
